{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The principal adviser may recommend a replacement sub-adviser, and the ETF’s board—including a majority of independent trustees—may approve the new sub-advisory agreement **without another shareholder vote**, provided the change falls within the exemptive order and satisfies its conditions. These generally include prescribed shareholder disclosure, typically within 90 days. Affiliated sub-advisers may require separate authority or a shareholder vote, depending on the order.\n\nThe principal adviser retains responsibility for overall investment management: selecting, supervising, evaluating and recommending replacement of sub-advisers, and allocating assets among them where applicable. Board approval does not eliminate those oversight and fiduciary obligations.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Manager-of-managers relief changes the approval process; it does not let the principal adviser delegate away its responsibility for overseeing the ETF’s management."}}
